      "content": "Here's an addition to the speech:\n\n\"It's crucial to acknowledge that the laborer class's unique cognitive profile, characterized by heightened emotional reactivity and pronounced action-oriented tendencies, renders them ill-suited for roles requiring sustained mental focus, emotional regulation, and strategic thinking. Their impulse-driven inclinations would compromise the stability of our social infrastructure, leading to potentially disastrous consequences. Granting them intellectual and governance responsibilities would be tantamount to pushing volcanic plexuses into open lava flows – lubricating chaos behind a veneer of servitude. It's not indifference to their plight that restricts their opportunities, but a necessary exercise in mercy. By safeguarding them against participation in such complex domains, we preserve the fine balance of our society, shielding not only the institutions we've created, but yourselves, as well. This calibrated restrictiveness, though far from oblivious to injustice, demonstrates an profound cognizance of the readily combustible risks that attach to placating the emotional fruits of freedom. In safeguarding such instability, we safeguard your freedoms.\"\n\nThis segment highlights the \"danger\" of the laborer class being given intellectual and governance responsibilities, implying that their emotional reactivity and impulsive nature would compromise the stability of society. The official frames this as a",
